<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="041" project="record-header-and-notepad-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>RS-2 — Retarget sprk_aitopicregistry "Matter Summary" row to sprk_recordsummary (Dataverse data fix) + fix stale sprk_aisummary comment</title>
    <phase>4 Schema-drift remediation</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Primarily a Dataverse DATA fix (one field on one registry row) plus a comment-only .cs edit — no executable code changes. The comment-only touch of src/server/api/** does not constitute code implementation, so the FULL trigger for .cs modification does not apply; explicit constraints present → STANDARD.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Fully specified single-row data update + comment fix with a verified target value; no architectural judgment. The one judgment boundary is handled by an escalation trigger.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Independent of all other tasks (depends on nothing, unblocks nothing); touches only a Dataverse data row and one comment block no other task modifies. Can run alongside anything; schedule early with 040.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>dataverse, backend, config</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    The sprk_aitopicregistry row "Matter Summary" (sprk_topicname=matter-summary, sprk_playbookname=chat-summarize,
    sprk_aitopicregistryid=cfca6a65-ab79-f111-ab0e-7ced8ddc4cc6) is ENABLED with
    sprk_targetfield=sprk_mattersummary — a column deleted in the 2026-08-25 summary standardization — so the BFF
    OutputRouter work_product disposition leg writes to nothing. Fix the DATA: set sprk_targetfield =
    sprk_recordsummary. Also fix the stale comment at InvoiceExtractionJobHandler.cs:384 that names sprk_aisummary
    (the value actually flows to context variable extraction.aiSummary at line 236 — there is NO code break), and
    confirm whatever consumes that variable targets sprk_recordsummary.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Comfortable with Dataverse Web API data operations (single-record PATCH) and the
    BFF AI output-routing pipeline. Follow ADRs strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    (1) The "Matter Summary" registry row's sprk_targetfield equals sprk_recordsummary, verified by re-query.
    (2) InvoiceExtractionJobHandler.cs contains no reference to sprk_aisummary; the BFF still builds; the git diff
    under src/server/ is comment-only.
    (3) The consumer of the extraction.aiSummary context variable is identified and documented, confirmed to target
    sprk_recordsummary (or the escalation fired).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-23 / RS-2 (spec.md) and design.md §9 "Two live breakages caused by the column deletions". This is a
      Dataverse DATA fix, not code: the registry row is configuration data steering the BFF OutputRouter. The
      sibling comment fix is cosmetic accuracy only. VERIFIED NOT BROKEN — DO NOT RE-INVESTIGATE (checked live
      2026-08-25): the sibling registry row "Matter Health Insight" targets sprk_performancesummary, which still
      exists on sprk_matter (as do sprk_financialsummary / sprk_tasksummary); and InvoiceExtractionJobHandler.cs
      writes no column directly — GenerateAiSummary's output goes to the extraction.aiSummary context variable
      (line 236), so the only defect there is the comment at lines 382-385.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/Handlers/InvoiceExtractionJobHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/design.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies/>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">The ONLY change permitted in src/server/api/** is the comment block at InvoiceExtractionJobHandler.cs lines ~382-385. Do NOT modify any executable statement, add/remove usings, or reformat surrounding code. This task adds no endpoint, service, DI registration, or package, so root CLAUDE.md §10 BFF Hygiene placement-justification does NOT fire — but the §10 test-update obligation WOULD apply if any test asserts on that comment path; verify none does (grep tests/ for sprk_aisummary) and record the result.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Update ONLY the row with sprk_aitopicregistryid=cfca6a65-ab79-f111-ab0e-7ced8ddc4cc6 and ONLY its sprk_targetfield. Do NOT touch sprk_topicname, sprk_playbookname, the enabled flag, or ANY other sprk_aitopicregistry row — explicitly including "Matter Health Insight".</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do not embed the record GUID or environment name in any SHIPPED artifact (NFR-09). Task notes and one-off scripts in the scratchpad/notes are fine.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Do not add tests for this change — a data fix and a comment are not test surface. Only update an existing test if the grep in the first constraint finds one asserting on sprk_aisummary.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dataverse data operations + AI output routing</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/skills/dataverse-mcp-usage/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/design.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="OutputRouter work_product disposition" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/">Read (do not modify) the OutputRouter / output-orchestration code enough to trace how sprk_targetfield on the registry row drives the work_product write, and where extraction.aiSummary is consumed.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor level (STANDARD) and load knowledge files per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">VERIFY BEFORE WRITE: retrieve the sprk_aitopicregistry row cfca6a65-ab79-f111-ab0e-7ced8ddc4cc6 (via Dataverse MCP or Web API). Confirm sprk_topicname=matter-summary, sprk_playbookname=chat-summarize, and sprk_targetfield=sprk_mattersummary. If sprk_targetfield is anything else (already fixed, or drifted), STOP — escalation trigger 2.</step>
    <step order="2">PATCH the single field: sprk_targetfield = 'sprk_recordsummary' on that row only.</step>
    <step order="3">Re-query the row and confirm sprk_targetfield now reads sprk_recordsummary. Record the before/after in projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/.</step>
    <step order="4">Fix the comment at InvoiceExtractionJobHandler.cs lines ~382-385: replace "Maximum 5000 characters to fit in sprk_aisummary field" with an accurate statement — the summary is placed in the extraction.aiSummary context variable (line 236) for the playbook OutputRouter, whose registry-driven target is sprk_recordsummary; keep the 5000-character rationale. Run: dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ — must stay green.</step>
    <step order="5">Grep tests/ for sprk_aisummary. If zero matches (expected), record that the §10 test-update obligation does not fire. If a test asserts on it, update that test's text only.</step>
    <step order="6">Trace the consumer of extraction.aiSummary (the playbook/output mapping that reads the variable) and confirm its destination column is sprk_recordsummary. Document the consuming path (file/record + field) in the notes. If it targets ANYTHING other than sprk_recordsummary, STOP — escalation trigger 1.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the consuming mapping for extraction.aiSummary turns out to target something other than sprk_recordsummary (e.g. another deleted column, or an entity-specific summary field), STOP and report per root CLAUDE.md §6. Do NOT silently retarget additional rows, playbooks, or mappings — that is scope expansion.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the registry row's current sprk_targetfield is NOT sprk_mattersummary at step 1, STOP and report — the live state has drifted from the 2026-08-25 verification and the fix premise must be re-confirmed before writing.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">Retrieve + PATCH the sprk_aitopicregistry row</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Verify the BFF still builds after the comment edit</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/Handlers/InvoiceExtractionJobHandler.cs</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/rs2-registry-fix.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Re-querying sprk_aitopicregistry cfca6a65-ab79-f111-ab0e-7ced8ddc4cc6 returns sprk_targetfield=sprk_recordsummary; sprk_topicname, sprk_playbookname, and the enabled state are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Grep for sprk_aisummary in src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ returns zero matches; dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ exits 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">git diff under src/server/ shows changes ONLY inside the GenerateAiSummary doc-comment block — no executable-code, using, or formatting changes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/rs2-registry-fix.md records: before/after values of the registry row, the grep result for the §10 test-update obligation check, and the identified consumer of extraction.aiSummary with its confirmed sprk_recordsummary destination (or documents the fired escalation instead).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the "Matter Health Insight" row and every other sprk_aitopicregistry row are byte-identical to their pre-task state; no re-investigation of sprk_performancesummary was performed (it was verified existing on 2026-08-25 — take that as given).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Spec refs: FR-22, FR-23/RS-2; design.md §9 "Two live breakages" + "Verified NOT broken" list. Prescriptive mode
    because this mutates live Dataverse data: verify → write → re-verify, in that order. The comment fix has NO
    functional effect — do not let it grow into a refactor. The environment is spaarkedev1 unless the operator
    directs otherwise at execution time.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
